    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "This is Hawaii Month\nMENU\nHilo Hattie",
      "Beverages\nPLEASE BE OUR GUEST:\nBOURBON\nWHISKIES\nSCOTCH\nTENNESSEE\nCANADIAN\nCOCKTAILS\nUNITED'S VERY DRY MARTINI\n(GIN OR VODKA)\nOLD FASHIONED\nMANHATTAN\nSCREWDRIVER\nBLOODY MARY\nMAI TAI\nDAIQUIRI\nWHISKEY SOUR\nSPANISH SHERRY\nGIN\nVODKA RUM\nBEER\n* * *\nTOMATO JUICE\nSOFT BEVERAGES\n* *\nHAWAIIAN MACADAMIA NUTS\nLIQUEURS\nCREME DE MENTHE\nBENEDICTINE AND BRANDY\nCOGNAC\nDRAMBUIE\nKAHLUA\nGALLIANO\nThe golden Italian cordial—a secret blend of herbs distilled, according to legend.\nfrom the rays of the sun.\nMinors Will Not Be Served Liquor.\nSelected American Wines are served with this menu.\nthe new yorker\nMenu\nOn board today's early New Yorker - first flight of the morning on the GREAT WIDE WAY\nTO New York - your breakfast needs are filled first.\nFRESH BERRIES IN SEASON WITH CREAM\nor\nCHILLED PINEAPPLE AND PAPAYA\nSELECTION OF FRUIT JUICES\nFOR YOUR BREAKFAST OR BRUNCH SELECTION:\nPOACHED EGGS, BERCY SAUCE\nCORNED BEEF PATTY\nor\nOMELETTE FINE HERBS\nor\nBROCHETTE OF BEEF, BERCY SAUCE\nHASH BROWNED POTATOES\nFROM THE SKILLET:\nBROILED BUFFET HAM\nGRILLED MEDALLION OF BEEF\nBROILED LINK SAUSAGE\nASSORTED BREAKFAST ROLLS AND CAKES\nLater, as your California clock passes high noon, we know you'll enjoy the many luncheon delights\nof our taste tempting Delicatessen, featuring:\nCREAM CHEESE. SMOKED SALMON\nSMOKED BEEF TONGUE, ROAST BEEF, HAM, CORNED BEEF AND\nCHOPPED CHICKEN LIVER\nGARNISHES\nASSORTED CHEESES AND CRACKERS\nA SELECTION OF BREADS AND ROLLS\nFollowed by a tempting\nDESSERT\nIt has been our pleasure to prepare this repast for your enjoyment.\nWilli Nicker\nWilli Niederer, Chef de cuisine\nUnited Air Lines Flight Kitchen at San Francisco International Airport\nMomkor Americon (niinory ederation\nMember, Chef de cuisine Association of the Pacific Coast\nPlease accept our apology if your choice is not available."
    ],
